{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-19T00:19:42.403Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1757"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1757: credential refusal next_steps tell agents to restore the redacted URL credentials before replay, which reproduces the same refusal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Reported in GH-1757 against 2026.11.18. When pm claim is refused because the author value is a URL that carries userinfo (via --author or PM_AUTHOR), the refusal correctly redacts the userinfo in recovery.attempted_command. But its next_steps tell the agent to restore the redacted credentials before replaying, and following that advice reproduces the byte-identical refusal. The guidance should instead steer to a replay that can succeed: an author value without URL credentials. The refusal-redaction work that introduced the redaction is related."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","claim","credential-redaction","gh:1757","recovery","refusal"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-19T00:19:42.403Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-19T00:19:42.403Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The refusal's next_steps never advise restoring redacted URL credentials when those credentials are the cause of the refusal; Following the emitted next_steps leads to a successful claim; Covered for both the --author flag and PM_AUTHOR"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-doxj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A refusal caused by URL credentials in the author value gives next_steps that lead to a successful replay, such as using an author value without URL credentials, and never advises restoring the redacted credentials."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"next_steps say to restore the redacted URL credentials before replaying; doing so reproduces the identical refusal, while a plain author retry succeeds."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-nhauur","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-19T00:19:42.403Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"26f95fa6aa1e557223a9dde33f5e507cb5918ad97a44d88575905359ae9f8cb0","item_hash_version":3,"message":"File GH-1757","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f727b899e3a24581f9a587bb2ed9f641afec55ece6d36268b74da94681e72ee0"}
