{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T05:12:59.393Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f719b3080f29d4118076bddd","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"release-operator","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1757","release:pm-gh1756"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-gh1757","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1757","release:pm-gh1756"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.329","source":"probe"}},"op":"close","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"claim --author with a credential URL now leads with the do-not-restore step plus Rerun with --author set to a plain name (JSON and text); PM_AUTHOR yields only Rerun with PM_AUTHOR set to a plain name, with an unredacted requirement; the plain-author replay claims the item with exit 0. Without the marker the GH-1757 spec fails; the full suite passes."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A refusal caused by URL credentials in an identity never advises restoring them, and following its next_steps leads to a successful claim, for both --author and PM_AUTHOR."},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/claim_principal"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/assignee"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T05:12:59.393Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"closed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/closed_at","value":"2026-11-20T05:12:59.373Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/completed_at","value":"2026-11-20T05:12:59.373Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/resolution","value":"The identity refusal declares the typed PmCliErrorContext marker url_credentials_rejected; redactGuidanceCredentials then leads with REJECTED_CREDENTIALS_STEP (the credentials caused this refusal, do not restore them, replay with a value that carries none) instead of the restore step. The refusal's requirement text no longer holds a credential-shaped sample, which redaction used to rewrite into user:[redacted]@ and count as a removed credential, so a PM_AUTHOR refusal carries only its plain-name step. contract_change and the SDK surface acknowledgement record the new optional key."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Identity refusals caused by URL credentials steer to a replay without them instead of advising their restoration"}],"before_hash":"065433202da52f092e9c3d9f1266112bfa4d98c31804d6c0d9cb21a28c01a015","after_hash":"c6bed4dc4bf427de5a7c52e06c15186540dd2e2c879f03efbb75a2f17631e532","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"completion":{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T05:12:59.373Z","source":"close_time"},"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"929528fbb7fa955bbeb635cc5817c2973511673746cbed162221036d451789e0"}
