{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T05:34:33.634Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f719b3080f29d4118076bddd","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.329","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-20T05:34:33.633Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review of the first head found the do-not-restore step over-attributed: with PM_AUTHOR carrying userinfo and an unrelated credential URL in a create description, the step claimed every redacted credential caused the refusal, and a bounded text rendering could keep it while dropping the PM_AUTHOR correction. The marker now carries its source (url_credentials_rejected: { source }), and the step names that source, gives the correction itself and still asks to restore any other redacted credentials. The integration spec covers that mixed case; the unit spec covers idempotence across a second redaction pass."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T05:34:33.634Z"}],"before_hash":"81f2bc7edd58dd95ee2c6306698d6ca924a75670fb28cb48fe81c305237b9d08","after_hash":"5b57ac255ddabe96bd8bb640597a69f74af3b858f96d33073a32d1d3f14e1e93","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d01ae30f3da6da39444f8c4e7bf59877b9b562154c3bdaf41956c195b356b4ff"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T05:34:46.776Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f719b3080f29d4118076bddd","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.329","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/contract_change/migrate","value":"Agents and clients matching the old restore-them step text for identity refusals should follow the source-specific step; producers whose refusal rejects URL credentials themselves set url_credentials_rejected: { source } on the PmCliError context"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/contract_change/after","value":"Such refusals set url_credentials_rejected: { source }; their first next step names that source, says its credentials caused the refusal and must not be restored, and asks to restore any other redacted credentials; a PM_AUTHOR refusal whose command line carries no credential has only the plain-name step"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T05:34:46.776Z"}],"before_hash":"5b57ac255ddabe96bd8bb640597a69f74af3b858f96d33073a32d1d3f14e1e93","after_hash":"f23ed7fa8da171dd76b9d95c159a6f97cbf450b5f38ad465159d023d91bbd083","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"60b3d7c5ddab9f56bbb512f6072346666a5be6485a175f4f56c6dd32b82de63d"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T05:51:56.792Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f719b3080f29d4118076bddd","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.329","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-20T05:51:56.792Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 2: a registered secret sharing a six-character fragment with the code-defined source label (for example one containing pm_author) made the second redaction pass, run by text rendering, rewrite the marker's source and build a different step. The urlCredentialsRejected marker is now copied whole like the fixed contract fields, so both passes build the identical step; PmCliErrorContext documents that source is a code-defined label, never caller input. Unit spec covers two passes under such a secret."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T05:51:56.792Z"}],"before_hash":"f23ed7fa8da171dd76b9d95c159a6f97cbf450b5f38ad465159d023d91bbd083","after_hash":"8eef872a65cc4d6912413d9ecd18451a58ca5db0aaf2ce0f7a43f3a48eaa7cb1","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1f441ce58bc4d76c29a187790051f8429c0b1e4f620a3d974cf3dc178859dcea"}
